Package: shr-rs
Version: %{VERSION}-1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: heavycaffeiner <146043537+heavycaffeiner@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/heavycaffeiner/shr-rs
Depends: mdadm, lvm2, parted, util-linux, curl, systemd
Recommends: btrfs-progs, smartmontools
Description: Sliced Hybrid RAID (SHR/SHR-2) manager over mdadm, LVM and Btrfs
 shr-rs manages SHR -- Sliced Hybrid RAID -- pools of mixed-capacity disks on
 the standard Linux stack. Disks are sliced into offset-aligned bands, each
 band becomes its own mdadm array, the arrays are concatenated by LVM, and
 Btrfs sits on top -- so disks of differing sizes contribute their full
 capacity and the array can be expanded online.
 .
 It provides create/expand with journaled rollback and crash resume, scrub
 (mdadm check plus Btrfs), disk replacement, SMART monitoring, transparent
 zstd recompression, snapshots with retention, an adaptive reshape throttle,
 and per-group systemd timers. Run it with no arguments for the interactive
 TUI, or with a subcommand for the scriptable CLI (add --json for
 schema-versioned machine-readable output).
 .
 Install cockpit-shr-rs for the web dashboard.
